WEBVTT

00:00:00.605 --> 00:00:01.470
Hello everyone.

00:00:01.824 --> 00:00:05.376
When a client walks into a salon, even before she sits down,

00:00:05.326 --> 00:00:07.710
she can feel whether the place is clean.

00:00:08.180 --> 00:00:11.870
But real cleanliness is not about a nice scent or beautiful lighting.

00:00:12.217 --> 00:00:17.230
It lies in small tasks, done regularly every day, and written down as a plan.

00:00:17.782 --> 00:00:22.030
Today we talk about daily salon cleaning, and the in-house control plan.

00:00:22.582 --> 00:00:27.151
I will use the guidance of the City of Helsinki, in Finland, as an example.

00:00:27.623 --> 00:00:30.831
In other countries and other cities, the rules will differ.

00:00:31.246 --> 00:00:33.311
But the way of thinking is almost the same.

00:00:33.910 --> 00:00:34.659
In Helsinki,

00:00:34.609 --> 00:00:39.960
most beauty salons must send a notification to the city at least 30 days before they start.

00:00:40.415 --> 00:00:44.440
Hair salons only have to notify if they also offer services on the skin.

00:00:44.948 --> 00:00:48.200
The same applies when working from home, or as a freelancer.

00:00:48.627 --> 00:00:52.280
A change of owner, or closing down, must also be reported.

00:00:52.682 --> 00:00:56.920
After that, the city carries out regular inspections, and charges a fee.

00:00:57.446 --> 00:00:58.996
Now the most important part:

00:00:59.192 --> 00:01:00.676
the in-house control plan.

00:01:01.016 --> 00:01:03.716
In Finnish, it is called omavalvonta.

00:01:03.958 --> 00:01:04.596
It means:

00:01:04.793 --> 00:01:07.989
the salon owner identifies the health risks in their own salon,

00:01:07.939 --> 00:01:10.436
and can show what they have done to prevent them.

00:01:10.758 --> 00:01:15.476
In Helsinki, every salon must have this plan, and must actually follow it.

00:01:15.742 --> 00:01:17.476
The city recommends writing it down.

00:01:17.739 --> 00:01:20.727
Hair salons, even if they do not have to notify,

00:01:20.677 --> 00:01:23.236
still have to carry out in-house control.

00:01:23.884 --> 00:01:25.172
What goes into the plan?

00:01:25.646 --> 00:01:27.652
First, a description of the salon:

00:01:27.838 --> 00:01:33.332
services, opening hours, number of people, sinks, toilets, equipment.

00:01:34.074 --> 00:01:38.212
Second, how tools are cleaned, disinfected and sterilized.

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:40.132
Third, the risks:

00:01:40.379 --> 00:01:44.609
sensitive clients, insects and rodents, things that need repair,

00:01:44.559 --> 00:01:46.372
and even times of epidemic.

00:01:46.790 --> 00:01:48.292
And fourth, prevention:

00:01:48.559 --> 00:01:52.612
staff instructions, a cleaning plan, and ventilation maintenance.

00:01:52.946 --> 00:01:55.732
When the salon changes, the plan is updated too.

00:01:56.349 --> 00:02:00.048
Tools, hand washing and incidents each have their own lesson.

00:02:00.310 --> 00:02:03.008
The lesson on processing tools after every client.

00:02:03.272 --> 00:02:05.488
The lesson on hand hygiene and gloves.

00:02:05.916 --> 00:02:07.168
And the lesson on incidents:

00:02:07.275 --> 00:02:10.288
bleeding, allergic reactions, burns.

00:02:10.795 --> 00:02:13.248
Today, we talk about the room itself:

00:02:13.323 --> 00:02:18.128
surfaces, floors, towels, water, air and waste.

00:02:18.767 --> 00:02:21.162
The cleaning plan should also be written down,

00:02:21.112 --> 00:02:23.507
and kept as part of the in-house control plan.

00:02:23.916 --> 00:02:24.867
Write clearly:

00:02:25.260 --> 00:02:30.547
what is cleaned, how often, with what equipment, with which product, and by whom.

00:02:31.095 --> 00:02:32.227
The first principle:

00:02:32.482 --> 00:02:37.667
clean first, then disinfect, because dirt makes disinfectant ineffective.

00:02:38.016 --> 00:02:41.587
Surfaces that do not touch the treated skin only need cleaning.

00:02:41.764 --> 00:02:45.747
Surfaces that touch the skin of the client are cleaned, then disinfected.

00:02:46.096 --> 00:02:49.582
And anywhere with blood on it, whether it touched the client or not,

00:02:49.532 --> 00:02:50.947
must always be disinfected.

00:02:51.474 --> 00:02:55.044
A schedule often seen in well run salons looks like this.

00:02:55.215 --> 00:02:56.404
After every client:

00:02:56.555 --> 00:02:59.455
the table, the arm rest, the chair, the lamp,

00:02:59.405 --> 00:03:01.924
and the places your hands have touched.

00:03:02.258 --> 00:03:03.524
At the end of every day:

00:03:03.790 --> 00:03:07.187
mop the floor, empty the bins, wipe the door handles,

00:03:07.137 --> 00:03:10.724
the taps and the reception desk, and wash the tool sink.

00:03:11.115 --> 00:03:11.844
Every week:

00:03:12.111 --> 00:03:16.644
cupboards, shelves, table legs, drawers, glass doors.

00:03:16.860 --> 00:03:18.644
How often you clean is your decision;

00:03:18.831 --> 00:03:19.844
then write it in the plan.

00:03:20.461 --> 00:03:22.500
Cleaning equipment must be clean too.

00:03:22.830 --> 00:03:27.556
According to the Helsinki guidance, cleaning cloths are washed after every use,

00:03:27.506 --> 00:03:28.740
at least 60 degrees,

00:03:28.830 --> 00:03:30.340
ideally 90 degrees.

00:03:30.445 --> 00:03:32.260
Or use disposable cloths.

00:03:32.606 --> 00:03:36.500
Mops and brooms are not left on the floor, and not stored in the toilet.

00:03:36.847 --> 00:03:38.740
There should be a separate cupboard with a door.

00:03:38.980 --> 00:03:42.733
The toilet has its own set of cleaning equipment, easy to tell apart,

00:03:42.683 --> 00:03:43.860
for example by color.

00:03:44.479 --> 00:03:48.432
Towels and textiles used at work are washed and dried by machine.

00:03:48.895 --> 00:03:51.312
The washing machine must not be placed in the toilet.

00:03:51.734 --> 00:03:54.032
Clean and dirty items are stored separately:

00:03:54.301 --> 00:03:58.352
clean towels in a closed cupboard, used towels in a bin with a lid.

00:03:58.852 --> 00:03:59.872
A common mistake:

00:04:00.141 --> 00:04:04.592
a stack of clean towels on an open shelf, right next to the basket of dirty ones.

00:04:05.237 --> 00:04:06.113
About water.

00:04:06.435 --> 00:04:11.438
Next to each workstation, or very close by, there must be a separate sink,

00:04:11.388 --> 00:04:13.312
for washing hands and tools,

00:04:13.368 --> 00:04:16.273
easy to reach, without passing through a closed door.

00:04:16.784 --> 00:04:21.393
If the salon has only one sink, it should be a double sink, with two basins.

00:04:21.765 --> 00:04:26.753
After washing tools, wash and disinfect the sink before using it again for clients.

00:04:26.979 --> 00:04:31.073
The toilet has its own hand basin, with liquid soap and paper towels.

00:04:31.727 --> 00:04:32.527
About air.

00:04:32.842 --> 00:04:34.527
Ventilation must be sufficient:

00:04:34.641 --> 00:04:39.007
according to the guidance, at least six liters of air per second, for each person.

00:04:39.753 --> 00:04:42.714
A salon with more than two clients at the same time,

00:04:42.664 --> 00:04:46.687
or using strong smelling chemicals, should have mechanical ventilation.

00:04:47.096 --> 00:04:49.647
An acrylic nail station needs local extraction.

00:04:49.887 --> 00:04:54.141
In the plan, write down the filter change schedule, the cleaning of the air vents,

00:04:54.091 --> 00:04:56.447
and the phone number of the building manager.

00:04:56.782 --> 00:04:58.687
And one thing that surprises many people:

00:04:58.956 --> 00:05:02.265
the guidance advises against potted plants in the salon,

00:05:02.215 --> 00:05:04.767
because soil holds a lot of microorganisms,

00:05:04.877 --> 00:05:07.007
and the air flow can carry them around the room.

00:05:07.663 --> 00:05:08.612
About waste.

00:05:08.897 --> 00:05:11.044
Bins must be intact, with a lid,

00:05:10.994 --> 00:05:14.452
and emptied often enough that the lid always closes.

00:05:14.718 --> 00:05:18.692
That way there is no smell, and no insects or rodents are attracted.

00:05:19.171 --> 00:05:23.339
Needles, blades and other sharps go into a factory made sharps container,

00:05:23.289 --> 00:05:25.652
and then to an approved collection point;

00:05:25.761 --> 00:05:28.452
in Helsinki, that is the Sortti stations.

00:05:28.554 --> 00:05:33.412
And if you see signs of insects or rodents, deal with them right away, do not wait.

00:05:33.956 --> 00:05:37.189
When the inspector comes, they do not only look at the tables.

00:05:37.519 --> 00:05:38.309
They may ask:

00:05:38.546 --> 00:05:42.549
what risks has the salon identified, and what has it done about them.

00:05:42.887 --> 00:05:47.187
A clearly written plan, and a salon that works exactly as the plan says,

00:05:47.137 --> 00:05:48.309
is the best answer.

00:05:48.925 --> 00:05:51.363
But a plan sitting in a drawer helps nobody.

00:05:51.753 --> 00:05:54.083
Turn it into two very short checklists.

00:05:54.243 --> 00:05:55.123
Morning opening:

00:05:55.461 --> 00:05:58.540
switch on the ventilation, test the hot and cold water,

00:05:58.490 --> 00:06:00.963
check there is enough soap and paper towels,

00:06:01.152 --> 00:06:04.483
that the sterile pouches are in date, and that the bins have been emptied.

00:06:04.957 --> 00:06:05.923
Evening closing:

00:06:06.092 --> 00:06:11.962
wipe the tables, mop the floor, wash the towels, empty the bins, wash the tool sink,

00:06:11.912 --> 00:06:13.763
and note anything unusual.

00:06:14.013 --> 00:06:16.163
Whoever does it ticks the box and signs.

00:06:16.432 --> 00:06:18.403
At the end of the week, the owner reviews it.

00:06:19.037 --> 00:06:19.624
You see.

00:06:19.979 --> 00:06:24.343
Salon hygiene is not one big spring clean, but small tasks every day,

00:06:24.293 --> 00:06:26.344
where everyone knows their part.

00:06:26.848 --> 00:06:30.264
Rules differ from country to country, and from city to city.

00:06:30.770 --> 00:06:32.584
Ask the health authority where you work.

00:06:32.838 --> 00:06:35.464
And now, take the short quiz below the video.
